The Herdr mods in herdr/mods/ (gonnawork-neon-tabs, gonnawork-neon-pane,
gonnawork-neon-agents, gonnawork-glass-files, gonnawork-glass-changes) are
modified copies of mods shipped with Herdr (https://github.com/herdrdev/herdr-app),
licensed under the Apache License 2.0. Changes: restyled for the neon/glass look;
neon-tabs adds Skills, Git, Stats and Ports panel buttons; neon-pane adds an
"Open in Ghostty" button; neon-agents shows Claude Code sub-agents as a tree;
glass-files draws VS Code style file icons; glass-changes has staged and unstaged
lists per repo and worktree. gonnawork-skills, gonnawork-stats, gonnawork-gitgraph
and gonnawork-ports are original.

The file and folder icons in herdr/mods/gonnawork-glass-files/icons/ are drawn
from Nerd Fonts glyphs (https://www.nerdfonts.com), which collect: Seti UI (MIT),
Material Design Icons (Apache License 2.0), Devicons (MIT), Font Awesome
(CC BY 4.0) and Octicons (MIT). Each file's name starts with its glyph set.

nvim/ is based on the LazyVim starter (https://github.com/LazyVim/starter),
licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
